"type":"hitted"}]},{"id":"401892492000001030","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Porter Martone hit Freddy Gaudreau","type":{"id":"503","text":"Hit","abbreviation":"hit"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:45"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"15"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5291941","displayName":"Porter Martone","shortName":"P. Martone"},"type":"hit-credited"},{"athlete":{"id":"3149649","displayName":"Frederick Gaudreau","shortName":"F. Gaudreau"},"type":"hitted"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1845","fullName":"Xfinity Mobile Arena","address":{"city":"Philadelphia","state":"PA","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1845.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17851,"officials":[{"fullName":"Francis Charron","displayName":"Francis Charron","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Ryan Jackson","displayName":"Ryan Jackson","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Liam Maaskant","displayName":"Liam Maaskant","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jeremy Faucher","displayName":"Jeremy Faucher","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Kraken beat Flyers 3-2 in shootout as Philadelphia’s winless start reaches 8 games","description":"— Bobby McMann scored a goal in regulation and then added the game-winner in the fifth round of the shootout as the Seattle Kraken beat the Philadelphia Flyers 3-2 on Tuesday night.","story":"PHILADELPHIA -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5048894/bobby-mcmann\">Bobby McMann</a> scored a goal in regulation and then added the game-winner in the fifth round of the shootout as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/sea/seattle-kraken\">Seattle Kraken</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/phi/philadelphia-flyers\">Philadelphia Flyers</a> 3-2 on Tuesday night. \n\n\r\n              The loss extended Philadelphia's franchise record for a winless streak to start a season to eight games (0-5-3).\n\n\r\n              McMann scored his third goal of the season on the power play in the first period when a loose puck bounced to him in the right circle, and he snapped a shot past Philadelphia goalie <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3942459/dan-vladar\">Dan Vladar</a>. He later beat Vladar in the shootout after Vladar made several nice stops to keep the Flyers' hopes alive. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5103811/ville-ottavainen\">Ville Ottavainen</a> scored his first NHL goal at 8:54 of the second period after the Flyers got caught with tired players on the ice following an icing call on defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080147/david-jiricek\">David Jiricek</a>.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5657/philipp-grubauer\">Philipp Grubauer</a> made 24 saves to earn the win for Seattle, which has won three straight road games. \n\n\r\n              Grubauer got into it with Flyers forward <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565230/trevor-zegras\">Trevor Zegras</a> on two successive plays in the second period. Zegras slashed Grubauer, and Grubauer responded with a cross-check. After Zegras came out of the box, Grubauer threw a puck at him; Zegras shot it back at him after the whistle, and they got into a skirmish again, and both were penalized. \n\n\r\n              Zegras beat Grubauer with a third-period goal as the Flyers evened the score with two goals. Grubauer got the better of Zegras, though, stoning him in the shootout.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3115035/christian-dvorak\">Christian Dvorak</a> also scored for Philadelphia and Vladar made 29 saves in defeat. \n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Kraken: Continue their five-game road trip Thursday at Tampa Bay.\n\n\r\n              Flyers: Travel to Detroit on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-14T02:29:29Z"}}